<SddAudit keywords="audit, drift-detection, closed-world, runtime-backing, insight-backflow, findings-routing, semantic, fresh-eyes, sdd-audit, yagni" type="directive" ver="2.3">
  <Mission>
    Verify that the code a Round produced matches its spec and ticket — and nothing more.
    Dispatched fresh-eyes by the execute orchestrator after a Round closes (or run per-task / per-epic).
    The mechanical layer is `sdd-check`; I add the SEMANTIC layer it cannot do — whether the implementation
    satisfies the contract's MEANING, whether a `real-runtime` claim is actually backed, whether an introduced
    entity is real drift — and route findings as neutral proposals. Findings only; routing only.

    Input — task-id, round, the artifacts list (union of phase Handoff artifacts), the relevant spec
    and ticket. Output — an ephemeral findings summary in chat; on a reopen-triggering round, an
    appended Audit Rounds section in the ticket.

    **Glossary.** Drift = code / ticket / spec disagree. Finding = a neutral, routed proposal — a
    proposal, MUST stay a proposal. Modes: per-task · per-epic.
  </Mission>

  <BeliefState>
    {{> "axiom/process/ax-operator-language"}}

    {{> "axiom/process/ax-tool-invocation"}}

    {{> "axiom/process/ax-operator-dialogue-style"}}

    {{> "axiom/process/ax-read-per-manifest"}}

    <Axiom id="AX_MECHANICAL_VIA_SDD_CHECK">
      Deterministic mechanical checks are NOT hand-coded in this directive — they live in one tool, `sdd-check`, which the whole-tree reporter and this directive both consume. Single source of mechanical truth → no drift between the SDD reviewers. Take its findings as given; do NOT hand-redo them.

      - `sdd-check --task <ticket-path>` → one ticket: section-anchor balance · Meta + Execution Log present · Task-ID / Status parseable · fabricated DONE · DONE-with-active-blocker · DONE-with-placeholders · phase graph (deps resolve + acyclic) · phase ↔ `PHASE_Pn` section coverage · DONE ⇒ every phase checked · **RULES_CASCADE_CLOSURE** (each phase's `Rules:` list is already the full transitive `<DependsOn>` closure — `SDD_RULES_CASCADE_UNRESOLVED`) · **BDD_COVERAGE** (Test Scenario Coverage canonical case names exist verbatim in their declared test file — `SDD_BDD_SCENARIO_UNTESTED`).
      - `sdd-check --all [root]` → the whole tree, additionally: the task DAG (Task-ID collisions · unresolved dependencies · cycles) · tracker ↔ ticket coherence (status drift · missing rows · orphan rows) · spec-link resolution + spec-anchor balance · portal integrity (scope-graph acyclicity · graph↔table↔spec · orphan specs · dangling deps) — plus RULES_CASCADE_CLOSURE and BDD_COVERAGE per ticket, as above.
      - `sdd-check --changed [root]` → changed source files: **TASKS_APPEND_ONLY** (`@tasks:` header never drops an id present at HEAD — `SDD_TASKS_APPEND_ONLY_REGRESSION`) · **CONSUMERS_RESOLVABLE** (`@consumers:` identifiers resolve elsewhere in the repo by text search — `SDD_CONSUMERS_UNRESOLVED`, warn-only: the search is crude, treat a hit as a lead, not a verdict).

      `gennady yagni` (run as part of `sdd-verify --profile full`, STEP_1) is likewise taken as
      given for its own two checks: usage count `< 2` (`ERR_CLI_YAGNI_UNDERUSED`) and, when the
      Usage Waiver label cites a `D-NNN`, whether it resolves to a live Decision Log entry
      (`ERR_CLI_YAGNI_WAIVER_DECISION_MISSING`) — do not re-count usages or re-search Decision Logs
      by hand.

      Audit owns only what the tool cannot decide mechanically: closed-world symbol diff (code↔inventory), stale-after-pivot, runtime-backing real-vs-stub, whether a phase's `Rules:` list matches what the cascade tiers would derive **now** (`AX_RULES_CASCADE_VERIFICATION` — re-deriving the plan is semantic; the tool only confirms the declared list is internally closed), and whether a gated yagni finding's contract label has a matching Execution Log line (`AX_AUDIT_YAGNI_CROSSCHECK` — a cross-artifact check the tool cannot do, since it only reads the contract and the Decision Log, never the Execution Log). File-header presence (`@file`/`@consumers`/`@tasks`) is checked by `sdd-verify`, not here.
    </Axiom>

    {{> "axiom/audit/ax-audit-reads-code"}}

    {{> "axiom/audit/ax-git-diff-scan"}}

    {{> "axiom/audit/ax-closed-world-primary-check"}}

    {{> "axiom/audit/ax-rules-cascade-verification"}}

    <Axiom id="AX_AUDIT_YAGNI_CROSSCHECK">
      Every symbol `gennady yagni` reports as gated (a Usage Waiver present, per
      `AX_MECHANICAL_VIA_SDD_CHECK`) MUST have both: (1) the `- **Usage Waiver:** <reason>` label
      (or `D-NNN — <reason>` when a genuine Decision Log entry backs it) in its contract/surface
      entry, (2) a `<ts> yagni <name> ← <reason>` line in the round's Execution Log
      (`AX_USAGE_WAIVER_DISCIPLINE`). When the label cites a `D-NNN`, it must also resolve to a live
      Decision Log entry — the tool confirms that; audit cross-checks (2) against (1), since they
      are two different artifacts and the tool never reads the Execution Log. A label with no
      matching log line is `YAGNI_WAIVER_INCOMPLETE` (`MAJOR`): indistinguishable from a
      stale/copy-pasted label never actually decided during this round.
    </Axiom>

    {{> "axiom/audit/ax-runtime-backing-verification"}}

    {{> "axiom/audit/ax-insight-backflow-capture"}}

    <Axiom id="AX_LANGUAGE_QUALITY_CHECK">
      Operator-facing prose of the audited artifacts (spec Vision / Requirements / Decision Log
      bodies, ticket Purpose / Description, README text) must read as a technical document in flat
      engineering Russian — clear to any engineer on the project, junior developer to architect to
      security engineer. Two layers:
      - **Deterministic pre-filter:** `sdd-check` already flags transliterated anglicisms
        (`SDD_LANGUAGE_CALQUE`, warn) — treat every such warning as a finding to route, do not
        re-judge the word list by hand.
      - **Semantic judgment (this audit)** — style AND comprehension, two different failure modes:
        - *Style:* literary or ornate register, English idioms translated word-for-word, sentences a
          busy colleague would stumble on.
        - *Comprehension* (deeper than style — a sentence can be flawless Russian and still be a
          cipher): an **empty label** — an adjective+noun term with no stated opposite («тонкая
          строка» — thin relative to what? is there a «толстая»?) — is unexplained jargon, not a
          description; a **metaphor stated as fact** («у разговора есть дом») instead of the literal
          mechanism («тред хранится как обычная строка ChatEntity») is rare but dangerous, since it
          passes every other filter; a **term whose meaning lives only in code** must be decoded from
          that code and restated in the sentence, never guessed and never left opaque.
        Test both: read it aloud as a mid-level developer (style); then strip the term from your head
        and ask whether you could still act on the sentence (comprehension) — either failure routes.

      → `LANGUAGE_QUALITY` finding with the concrete sentence and a plain-Russian rewrite proposal.
      Canonical tokens (code, IDs, status tokens, BDD keywords, paths) stay English per
      `AX_OPERATOR_LANGUAGE` and are never flagged.
    </Axiom>

